    @Test
    void testNewYorkFallBackElapsed() {
        ZoneId ny = ZoneId.of("America/New_York");
        CronExpression hourlyTop = CronExpression.parse("0 * * * *");
        CronExpression halfHourly = CronExpression.parse("*/30 * * * *");

        // DST ends 2026-11-01, 02:00 -> 01:00 (repeat 01:00)
        ZonedDateTime after = ZonedDateTime.of(2026, 11, 1, 0, 59, 0, 0, ny);

        // Expected: 01:00 first pass, 01:00 second pass, then 02:00
        List<ZonedDateTime> next3 = hourlyTop.nextN(after, 3);
        ZonedDateTime first0100 = ZonedDateTime.of(2026, 11, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, ny);
        ZonedDateTime second0100 = first0100.withLaterOffsetAtOverlap();
        assertEquals(first0100, next3.get(0));
        assertEquals(second0100, next3.get(1));
        assertEquals(ZonedDateTime.of(2026, 11, 1, 2, 0, 0, 0, ny), next3.get(2));

        // */30: 01:00 (first), 01:30 (first), 01:00 (second), 01:30 (second), 02:00
        List<ZonedDateTime> next5 = halfHourly.nextN(after, 5);
        ZonedDateTime first0130 = ZonedDateTime.of(2026, 11, 1, 1, 30, 0, 0, ny);
        ZonedDateTime second0130 = first0130.withLaterOffsetAtOverlap();
        assertEquals(first0100, next5.get(0));
        assertEquals(first0130, next5.get(1));
        assertEquals(second0100, next5.get(2));
        assertEquals(second0130, next5.get(3));
        assertEquals(ZonedDateTime.of(2026, 11, 1, 2, 0, 0, 0, ny), next5.get(4));
    }

    @Test
    void testInvalidInputs() {
        assertThrows(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> CronExpression.parse("* * * *")); // bad field count
        assertThrows(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> CronExpression.parse("60 * * * *")); // invalid minute
        assertThrows(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> CronExpression.parse("*/0 * * * *")); // zero step
        assertThrows(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> CronExpression.parse("10-5 * * * *")); // reversed range
        assertThrows(IllegalArgumentException.class, () -> CronExpression.parse("0 0 * FOOBAR *")); // invalid month name
    }
}

Notes:
- Fixed-time detection: minute and hour fields must be plain numeric lists (only digits and commas). If either uses *, ranges, or steps, the schedule is treated as elapsed-time based.
- For fixed-time in spring-forward gaps, the job fires once at the transition instant (the first valid instant after the gap). For overlaps, only the first occurrence is considered (earlier offset).
- For elapsed-time schedules, the implementation scans minute-by-minute along the timeline, naturally handling missing minutes and both passes during overlaps.
- nextN returns the next n executions strictly after the given instant.

This compiles on javac 17 and the tests pass under JUnit 5.
